## 2. The 10-Step Generic Incubation Framework **[core gate]**

Use this structured checklist to evaluate any new startup hypothesis or wedge before approving engineering effort:

| Step | Gate | Key Question & Validation Criteria |
|---|---|---|
| **1** | **User** | Who specifically feels the pain, what is their exact role/job title, and how often do they encounter it? |
| **2** | **Pain** | What is broken, slow, expensive, risky, inaccessible, or emotionally frustrating right now? |
| **3** | **Existing Behavior** | What hacks, spreadsheets, manual copy-pasting, or poorly stitched legacy tools are they currently using? |
| **4** | **Why Now** | What exact catalyst changed recently in technology capabilities, regulation, cloud billing costs, or distribution channels? |
| **5** | **Solution** | What precise workflow or capability becomes possible today that was impossible or economically unfeasible 2 years ago? |
| **6** | **Wedge** | What narrow, underserved beachhead segment can you dominate first before expanding? |
| **7** | **Moat** | What asset compounds over time as usage scales: data gravity, workflow memory, trust/audit logs, integrations, or distribution networks? |
| **8** | **Business Model** | Who signs the check, how is pricing metered (per seat, per transaction, per infrastructure saving), and what drives expansion? |
| **9** | **Validation** | What concrete evidence validates willingness to pay: pre-orders, LOIs, active manual prototypes, or high churn/complaints on existing alternatives? |
| **10** | **Scale Path** | How does winning the initial narrow wedge naturally unlock adjacent product categories or horizontal TAM expansion? |

