## 3. Ten Commandments for Startup Ideation **[mindset]**

1. Start with a painful user truth, never with a solution searching for a problem.
2. Make the problem description specific enough that the target user instantly feels seen.
3. Articulate precisely why existing tools structurally fail, not just why your feature list is longer.
4. Claim and win a sharp, narrow beachhead before boasting about a multi-billion-dollar TAM.
5. Build smoothly around an existing, habitual user workflow instead of demanding behavior change.
6. Use AI specifically to eliminate bottlenecks: institutional memory, complex decisions, verification, speed, or skill gaps.
7. Always design for a compounding asset: an evolving graph, cryptographic audit trail, custom fine-tuned model, or historical benchmark.
8. Make the **"Why Now?"** undeniable; market timing and technical feasibility catalysts are the ultimate multipliers.
9. Demonstrate a believable, high-margin path to monetization, not just vanity metrics or engagement.
10. Anchor the concept with a crisp founder insight: why you see the market shift before others, and why your technical background makes you uniquely qualified to build it.

